  "notes": "West leads the ♥5 against 3NT. West's lead is in response to his partner's weak 2 bid. Holding up the ♥A cannot cost, but it also cannot gain as East has shown exactly 6 hearts and it will be impossible to exhaust all 3 of West's hearts.\n\nThere are 8 top tricks (3 spades, the ♥A, the ♦A, and 3 clubs). If West has the ♦K, it will be possible to make several overtricks by finessing in that suit. South should limit his aspirations to 9 tricks and concentrate on simply making his contract.\n\nIf either spades or clubs divide 3-3 a ninth trick will be available without risking the diamond finesse.\n\nAfter winning the heart lead, South should begin by cashing the top honours in spades and clubs. When neither of these suits divide favourably, South must fall back on the diamond finesse.",
